Day 47 - Rotate List

Problem Statement:
Given the head of a linked list, rotate the list to the right by k places.

Code
class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* rotateRight(ListNode* head, int k) {
        if (head == NULL || head->next == NULL || k == 0) {
            return head;
        }


        int n = 1;
        ListNode* temp = head;


        while (temp->next != NULL) {
            temp = temp->next;
            n++;
        }


        temp->next = head;


        k = k % n;
        int step = n - k;


        ListNode* newTail = head;


        for (int i = 1; i < step; i++) {
            newTail = newTail->next;
        }


        ListNode* newHead = newTail->next;


        newTail->next = NULL;


        return newHead;
    }
};




Time Complexity:
O(n)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
First, the length n of the linked list is calculated while reaching the last node. The last node is then connected to the head, temporarily converting the linked list into a circular linked list. Since rotating by n positions produces the same list, k is reduced using k = k % n. The new tail will be at position n - k, so we move newTail to that position. The node after newTail becomes the new head, and finally, the circular connection is broken by setting newTail->next = NULL. This rotates the list in O(n) time using O(1) extra space.
